{"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"FoundationEssentials defines the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/FormatStyle","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" protocol to establish conventions for formatting a given type as some kind of output type, typically a ","type":"text"},{"code":"String","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Similarly, the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/ParseStrategy","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" protocol provides an API for converting a representation back to the represented type, such as converting a numeric string to an ","type":"text"},{"code":"Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/Decimal","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"While FoundationEssentials defines the core protocols, most implementations of ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/FormatStyle","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/ParseStrategy","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" exist in the ","type":"text"},{"code":"FoundationInternationalization","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" module.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"FoundationInternationalization","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" also extends types in both ","type":"text"},{"code":"FoundationEssentials","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and the Swift Standard Library to add formatting and parsing support.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"When you import ","type":"text"},{"code":"FoundationInternationalization","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", you have two general approaches to perform formatting of supported types:","type":"text"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Call ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"formatted()"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"formatted(_:)"},{"text":" on an instance of the type, optionally passing in a customized ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FormatStyle"},{"text":" appropriate to the type. These methods, defined by extensions in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FoundationInternationalization"},{"type":"text","text":", are useful for performing one-off formatting with default styles or slightly-customized styles. For example, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"var string123 = Double(1.23).formatted()"},{"type":"text","text":" creates the string "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"1.23"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Call ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"format(_:)"},{"text":" on an instance of the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FormatStyle"},{"text":", passing in the type you want to format. This method, defined by the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FormatStyle"},{"text":" itself, makes sense when you customize a style and want to format many instances with it. For example, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"var string456 = FloatingPointFormatStyle<Double>().format(4.56)"},{"text":" creates the string ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"4.56"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The arrangement is similar with parsing:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Call "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"init(strategy:)"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"init(_:format:lenient:)"},{"text":" to create instance of a type from its formatted representation. For example, to create a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Double","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" from the string ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"1.23"},{"text":", you could use ","type":"text"},{"code":"var oneTwoThree = try Double(\"1.23\", format: FloatingPointFormatStyle<Double>())","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Call ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"parse(_:)"},{"text":" on an instance of the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ParseStrategy"},{"text":" to initialize an instance of the output type. For example, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"var fourFiveSix = try FloatingPointFormatStyle<Double>().parseStrategy.parse(\"4.56\")"},{"text":" creates a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Double"},{"text":" equal to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"4.56"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]}]}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/DataFormatting"},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/FormatStyle","doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/DiscreteFormatStyle","doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/ParseableFormatStyle"],"title":"Data formatting","anchor":"Data-formatting"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/ParseableFormatStyle","doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/ParseStrategy"],"title":"Data parsing","anchor":"Data-parsing"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/Locale"],"title":"Internationalization